     "content": "```python\ndef roman_to_int(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a Roman numeral string to an integer.\n    Supports standard and subtractive notation (IV, IX, XL, XC, CD, CM).\n    \"\"\"\n    roman_map = {\n        'I': 1,\n        'V': 5,\n        'X': 10,\n        'L': 50,\n        'C': 100,\n        'D': 500,\n        'M': 1000\n    }\n\n    total = 0\n    n = len(s)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_value = roman_map[s[i]]\n\n        # Check if there is a next character and if the current value is less than the next\n        if i < n - 1:\n            next_value = roman_map[s[i+1]]\n            if current_value < next_value:\n                # Subtractive case (e.g., IV, IX)\n                total -= current_value\n            else:\n                # Additive case\n                total += current_value\n        else:\n            # Last character, always add its value\n            total += current_value\n\n    return total\n```",
